    "updated_at": "2016-02-25T22:40:19Z",
    "body": "I am still a bit confused about this. Please let me know if I am misunderstanding.\n\nThe situation we are concerned about (from #704 and https://jsfiddle.net/4f9a3ucq/) falls under the following, right?\n\n> When the currently focused area of a top-level browsing context was a focusable area but stops being a focusable area, or when it was a dialog in a dialog group and stops being part of that dialog group, or when it starts being inert, the user agent must run the following steps:\n\n(I wish this had a linkable anchor.)\n\nIn this case:\n- step 1 will set _old focus target_ to the now-hidden ul\n- step 2 will set _old chain_ to the focus chain starting at the now-hidden ul, to its parent li, to the parent document\n- step 3 will run the focus fixup rules. With your new focus fixup rule 1:\n  - I am confused what the control group is exactly?\n  - There is no longer a focused area of the control group. This seems probably true.\n  - It sets the sequential focus navigation starting point to the old focused area, since it still exists (maybe this should be more precise \"in a Document\"?? Or in the same document as the control group owner?????)\n- Step 4 sets _new focus target_ to the currently focused area of a top-level browsing context. But we just established that there is no focused area of the control group, so the return value will be the document.\n- Step 5 compares the hidden ul to the document, so it proceeds.\n- Step 6 sets _new chain_ to be the chain consisting of just the document.\n- Step 7 runs the focus update steps.\n  - Step 1 of the focus update steps **unsets the sequential focus navigation starting point**, so our work in focus fixup step one is undone.\n\nThings seem to have gone wrong.\n\nThis stuff is complicated and the spec's existing phrasing is not easy for me to understand. So it's quite possible I am missing something. But my intuition is that the focus fixup rules are probably OK as they are, and the change needs to happen by changing the first step of the focus update steps to no longer unset the sequential focus navigation starting point.\n\nIt would help if I had a better idea what the control groups actually are. The spec says each focusable area belongs to a control group, but doesn't really give any examples. Maybe I will file a separate bug on that.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
